---
title: Saga compensation - fulfillment failure and customer cancellation
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant O as order-service
  participant K as Kafka
  participant I as inventory-service
  participant F as fulfillment-service
  participant R as SagaRecoveryJob
  Note over O,F: Case A - fulfillment fails after its own retries
  F->>K: FulfillmentFailed (attempts=3)
  K->>O: FulfillmentFailed
  O->>O: CONFIRMED to COMPENSATION_PENDING, saga COMPENSATING reason FULFILLMENT_FAILURE
  O->>K: ReleaseInventory (via outbox)
  K->>I: ReleaseInventory
  I->>I: reservation RELEASED, reserved decreases (shipped goods are never released)
  I->>K: InventoryReleased
  K->>O: InventoryReleased
  O->>O: COMPENSATION_PENDING to FAILED, saga COMPENSATED, OrderFailed event
  Note over O,I: Case B - customer cancels a confirmed order
  O->>O: POST cancel: CONFIRMED to COMPENSATION_PENDING (reason CANCELLATION)
  O->>K: ReleaseInventory
  K->>I: ReleaseInventory
  I->>K: InventoryReleased
  K->>O: InventoryReleased, order CANCELLED, OrderCancelled event
  Note over O,R: Case C - InventoryReleased never arrives
  R->>O: finds saga stuck longer than stuck-after-seconds
  R->>K: re-send ReleaseInventory (idempotent receiver)
  R->>O: after max-attempts: saga NEEDS_ATTENTION, order stays COMPENSATION_PENDING, alert metric
  Note over O: Admin retry or ReconciliationService re-opens it
